**Improvement:** These three methods are essentially the same pattern. Consider creating a private helper `getLineObject(int row)` that returns the TerminalRow after conversion:
```java
private TerminalRow getLineObject(int row) {
    return mLines[externalToInternalRow(row)];
}
```

---

### 10. **Repeated if/else with getLineWrap() check** (TerminalBuffer.java)
**Lines:** 85-94  
**Pattern:**
```java
boolean rowLineWrap = getLineWrap(row);
if (rowLineWrap && x2 == columns) {
    lastPrintingCharIndex = x2Index - 1;
} else {
    for (i = x1Index; i < x2Index; ++i) {
        char c = line[i];
        if (c != ' ') lastPrintingCharIndex = i;
    }
